{"skill_id":"cs-intro","version":1,"questions":[{"id":"cs-intro-r1-q1","round":1,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A CS stage has \\(V_{DD} = 1.8\\ \\mathrm{V}\\), \\(R_D = 5\\ \\mathrm{k\\Omega}\\), \\(\\mu_nC_{ox}W/L = 2\\ \\mathrm{mA/V^2}\\), \\(V_T = 0.5\\ \\mathrm{V}\\) and \\(V_{GS} = 0.8\\ \\mathrm{V}\\). Assuming saturation, find the DC output voltage in V.","answer":1.35,"unit":"V","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"\\(I_D = \\tfrac12(2\\ \\mathrm{mA/V^2})(0.3)^2 = 90\\ \\mu\\mathrm{A}\\), so \\(V_{out} = 1.8 - (90\\ \\mu\\mathrm{A})(5\\ \\mathrm{k\\Omega}) = 1.35\\ \\mathrm{V}\\). Using \\(V_{GS}\\) instead of \\(V_{ov}\\) in the square law, or forgetting the \\(\\tfrac12\\), gives a wrong current (reader Sec. 9.2).","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 214\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Common-source amplifier: NMOS with load R_D to the supply.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:260px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"118\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"142\" y2=\"20\"/><text x=\"130\" y=\"15\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_DD</text><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"20\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"34\"/><polyline points=\"130,34 130,41 124,44 136,49 124,54 136,59 124,64 136,69 130,77 130,84\"/><text x=\"142\" y=\"63\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">R_D</text><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"84\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"96\"/><line x1=\"104\" y1=\"108\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"140\"/><line x1=\"84\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"104\" y2=\"124\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"106\" x2=\"110\" y2=\"142\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"112\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"112\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"96\"/><line x1=\"110\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"136\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"152\"/><line x1=\"128\" y1=\"136\" x2=\"114\" y2=\"136\"/><polygon points=\"114,136 119.5,133.7 119.5,138.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"96\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"138\" y=\"90\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">v_out</text><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"96\" x2=\"190\" y2=\"96\"/><circle cx=\"190\" cy=\"96\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><text x=\"196\" y=\"100\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"></text><line x1=\"84\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"124\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"124\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"137\"/><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"161\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"174\"/><circle cx=\"60\" cy=\"149\" r=\"12\"/><text x=\"60\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">+</text><text x=\"60\" y=\"159\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">−</text><text x=\"43\" y=\"153\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">v_in</text><line x1=\"60\" y1=\"174\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"180\"/><line x1=\"51\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"69\" y2=\"180\"/><line x1=\"55\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"65\" y2=\"184\"/><line x1=\"58.5\" y1=\"188\" x2=\"61.5\" y2=\"188\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"152\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"170\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"170\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"176\"/><line x1=\"121\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"139\" y2=\"176\"/><line x1=\"125\" y1=\"180\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"180\"/><line x1=\"128.5\" y1=\"184\" x2=\"131.5\" y2=\"184\"/></svg>","figure_alt":"Common-source amplifier: NMOS with load R_D to the supply."},{"id":"cs-intro-r1-q2","round":1,"type":"mc","prompt":"As \\(V_{in}\\) rises from 0 to \\(V_{DD}\\), how does the CS output move?","options":["It rises steadily from 0 to \\(V_{DD}\\)","It falls linearly over the whole range","It falls only after the device enters triode","It stays at \\(V_{DD}\\) until \\(V_T\\), falls steeply while the device is saturated, then flattens near 0 in triode"],"correct_index":3,"explanation":"Below \\(V_T\\) no current flows, so there is no drop across \\(R_D\\). Once on, \\(I_DR_D\\) grows with \\(V_{ov}^2\\) and the output falls fast; when the drain drops below \\(V_{ov}\\) the device acts like a resistor and the curve flattens. The stage is inverting, so it never rises.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Common-source DC transfer curve: output stays at V_DD until the input reaches V_T, falls steeply while the transistor is saturated, then flattens toward zero once it enters triode.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_in (V)</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_out (V)</text><polyline points=\"50,41 52.2,41 54.5,41 56.8,41 59,41 61.2,41 63.5,41 65.8,41 68,41 70.2,41 72.5,41 74.8,41 77,41 79.2,41 81.5,41 83.8,41 86,41 88.2,41 90.5,41 92.8,41 95,41 97.2,41 99.5,41 101.8,41 104,41 106.2,41 108.5,41 110.8,41 113,41.2 115.2,41.5 117.5,41.9 119.8,42.6 122,43.4 124.2,44.4 126.5,45.5 128.8,46.9 131,48.3 133.2,50 135.5,51.8 137.8,53.8 140,56 142.2,58.3 144.5,60.8 146.8,63.5 149,66.4 151.2,69.4 153.5,72.5 155.8,75.9 158,79.4 160.2,83.1 162.5,86.9 164.8,91 167,95.1 169.2,99.5 171.5,104 173.8,108.7 176,113.6 178.2,118.6 180.5,123.8 182.8,129.2 185,134.8 187.2,140 189.5,143.2 191.8,145.4 194,147.1 196.2,148.6 198.5,149.8 200.8,150.9 203,151.8 205.2,152.7 207.5,153.5 209.8,154.2 212,154.9 214.2,155.5 216.5,156.1 218.8,156.6 221,157.1 223.2,157.6 225.5,158 227.8,158.4 230,158.8 232.2,159.2 234.5,159.5 236.8,159.9 239,160.2 241.2,160