ompt":"\\(V_{DD} = 1.8\\ \\mathrm{V}\\), \\(R_D = 10\\ \\mathrm{k\\Omega}\\), \\(\\mu_nC_{ox}W/L = 1\\ \\mathrm{mA/V^2}\\), \\(V_T = 0.4\\ \\mathrm{V}\\). At what input voltage (in V) does the CS output reach the saturation edge, \\(V_{out} = V_{ov}\\)? (The region condition is the prerequisite step; the skill here is solving the transfer curve.)","answer":0.908276,"unit":"V","tolerance":0.01,"explanation":"Set \\(1.8 - 10\\ \\mathrm{k\\Omega}\\cdot\\tfrac12(1\\ \\mathrm{mA/V^2})V_{ov}^2 = V_{ov}\\): \\(5V_{ov}^2 + V_{ov} - 1.8 = 0\\), so \\(V_{ov} \\approx 0.508\\ \\mathrm{V}\\) and \\(V_{in} \\approx 0.908\\ \\mathrm{V}\\). This is the knee in the transfer curve; beyond it the gain collapses.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Common-source DC transfer curve: output stays at V_DD until the input reaches V_T, falls steeply while the transistor is saturated, then flattens toward zero once it enters triode.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_in (V)</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_out (V)</text><polyline points=\"50,41 52.2,41 54.5,41 56.8,41 59,41 61.2,41 63.5,41 65.8,41 68,41 70.2,41 72.5,41 74.8,41 77,41 79.2,41 81.5,41 83.8,41 86,41 88.2,41 90.5,41 92.8,41 95,41 97.2,41 99.5,41 101.8,41 104,41 106.2,41 108.5,41 110.8,41 113,41.2 115.2,41.5 117.5,41.9 119.8,42.6 122,43.4 124.2,44.4 126.5,45.5 128.8,46.9 131,48.3 133.2,5