ut stays at V_DD until the input reaches V_T, falls steeply while the transistor is saturated, then flattens toward zero once it enters triode."},{"id":"cs-intro-r3-q3","round":3,"type":"numeric","prompt":"A CS device (\\(\\mu_nC_{ox}W/L = 2\\ \\mathrm{mA/V^2}\\)) is biased at \\(V_{ov} = 0.2\\ \\mathrm{V}\\) and the input carries a 50 mV-peak sine. What is the drain current at the positive input peak, in µA? (This large swing shows why bias must be chosen with the signal size in mind.)","answer":62.5,"unit":"µA","tolerance":0.02,"explanation":"\\(V_{ov}\\) peaks at 0.25 V: \\(I_D = \\tfrac12(2\\ \\mathrm{mA/V^2})(0.25)^2 = 62.5\\ \\mu\\mathrm{A}\\). At the negative peak it is 22.5 µA, so the 40 µA bias swings +22.5/−17.5 µA: visibly distorted.","figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 340 210\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Saturation drain current versus gate-source voltage: zero below threshold V_T, then a parabola in the overdrive.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:340px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"330\" y2=\"176\"/><polygon points=\"330,176 323.6,178.7 323.6,173.3\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"50\" y1=\"176\" x2=\"50\" y2=\"16\"/><polygon points=\"50,16 52.7,22.4 47.3,22.4\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\"/><text x=\"330\" y=\"192\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_GS (V)</text><text x=\"54\" y=\"12\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">I_D (sat)</text><polyline points=\"50,176 52.2,176 54.5,176 56.8,176 59,176 61.2,176 63.5,176 65.8,176 68,176 70.2,176 72.5,176 74.8,176 77,176 79.2,176 81.5,176 83.8,176 86,176 88.2,176 90.5,176 92.8,176 95,176 97.2,176 99.5,176 101.8,176 104,176 106.2,176 108.5,176 110.8,176 113,176 115.3,176 117.5,176 119.8,176 122,176 124.3,176 126.5,176 128.8,176 131,176 133.2