wn at the bias point; the tangent's slope is the transconductance g_m."},{"id":"cs-intro-r4-q2","round":4,"type":"mc","prompt":"Preview of coupling: the signal source sits at 0 V DC but the gate must sit at 0.8 V. What is the usual fix?","options":["Connect the source directly; the gate will find 0.8 V","Add a resistor in series with the source","Raise \\(V_{DD}\\)","Couple the signal through a capacitor and set the gate's DC level with a separate bias network"],"correct_index":3,"explanation":"A direct connection forces the gate to 0 V and the device turns off. A capacitor blocks DC so the bias network sets the gate while the signal passes.","preview":["bias-coupling"],"figure":"<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 156\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Gate bias network: divider R_1 from the supply and R_2 to ground sets the gate's DC voltage; the signal source v_s connects to the gate through coupling capacitor C_c.\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" font-family=\"sans-serif\" font-size=\"12\" style=\"max-width:260px;width:100%;height:auto\"><line x1=\"108\" y1=\"14\" x2=\"132\" y2=\"14\"/><text x=\"120\" y=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-size=\"11\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">V_DD</text><polyline points=\"120,14 120,21 114,24 126,29 114,34 126,39 114,44 126,49 120,57 120,64\"/><text x=\"132\" y=\"43\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">R_1</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"64\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"84\"/><polyline points=\"120,84 120,91 114,94 126,99 114,104 126,109 114,114 126,119 120,127 120,134\"/><text x=\"132\" y=\"113\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">R_2</text><line x1=\"120\" y1=\"134\" x2=\"120\" y2=\"140\"/><line x1=\"111\" y1=\"140\" x2=\"129\" y2=\"140\"/><line x1=\"115\" y1=\"144\" x2=\"125\" y2=\"144\"/><line x1=\"118.5\" y1=\"148\" x2=\"121.5\" y2=\"148\"/><circle cx=\"120\" cy=\"74\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"